# .secrets-local — strings this repo must never publish.  COPY TO `.secrets-local`,
# which is gitignored.  This file is the TEMPLATE and is tracked; the real one is not,
# because a denylist in the repo publishes exactly what it exists to protect.
#
# One string per line, matched case-insensitively as a substring by
# .githooks/scan-identifiers.sh.  MAC/BSSID addresses need no entry — they are matched
# by shape, so they are caught from a fresh clone with no setup.
#
# Put here anything with no recognisable shape:
#   - your wifi SSID
#   - a hostname or account name you would not put on a public repo
#   - a static/public IP (RFC1918 addresses like 10.0.0.x are deliberately NOT flagged;
#     they appear all over these docs legitimately and blocking them would be noise)
#
# Uncomment and replace with your own — do NOT put a real value in this TRACKED template.
# (Writing one here is the exact mistake this whole mechanism exists to stop, and the
#  first draft of this file did it: the example was the author's own live SSID.)
# my-wifi-name
